dnl ============================================================
dnl mod_event_agent integration snippet for FreeSWITCH configure.ac
dnl ============================================================
dnl
dnl Drop these blocks into the FreeSWITCH `configure.ac` when you
dnl install this module in-tree at:
dnl     freeswitch/src/mod/applications/mod_event_agent/
dnl
dnl Two minimal edits to FS upstream:
dnl
dnl   1) Near the top of configure.ac, after the existing PKG_CHECK_*
dnl      block (search for "PKG_CHECK_MODULES" and append):
dnl
dnl        m4_include([src/mod/applications/mod_event_agent/m4/ax_lib_nats.m4])
dnl        PKG_CHECK_MODULES([CJSON], [libcjson >= 1.7])
dnl        AX_LIB_NATS
dnl
dnl   2) At the bottom of configure.ac, in the AC_CONFIG_FILES list
dnl      that lists every module's Makefile, add:
dnl
dnl        src/mod/applications/mod_event_agent/Makefile
dnl
dnl   3) Activate the module on installs by adding a line to
dnl      build/modules.conf.in:
dnl
dnl        applications/mod_event_agent
dnl
dnl After those three edits:
dnl     ./bootstrap.sh && ./configure && make && sudo make install
dnl
dnl …drops mod_event_agent.so into $prefix/freeswitch/mod/ alongside
dnl the rest of FS, and `load mod_event_agent` works on next start.
dnl
dnl The libcjson and libnats checks are mandatory because the module
dnl will not link without them. Operators who prefer a Kafka or other
dnl driver can extend the AC_DEFUN([AX_LIB_NATS]) pattern in m4/ to
dnl detect their backend and add a parallel `if HAVE_KAFKA` block in
dnl the Makefile.am.
